<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ubar-Tutu</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ubar-Tutu is the last king before the flood in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumerian-king-list">Sumerian King List</a>, said to have ruled at Shuruppak for thousands of years. Some versions of the flood tradition make him the father of the flood hero <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ziusudra">Ziusudra</a>, called Utnapishtim in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/epic-of-gilgamesh">Epic of Gilgamesh</a>. He is a figure of legend, not a historically attested ruler.</p></div>
